-- #822 S0 REGRESSION PIN (adversarial review of PR #1011).  Declaring a graded
-- interface must leave the PRELUDE typed exactly as it always was.
--
-- The first cut of #822 published `f ↦ [KRow]` under the bare name, which collides
-- with every arity-1 `f a` in Mappable / Applicative / Thenable / Foldable, so this
-- four-line file produced 45 `Type mismatch` and `No impl` errors — all of them
-- mislocated at the user's own `interface` line, none of them mentioning the prelude.
--
-- ⚠️ COVERAGE GAP (#2033, 2026-08-26): this golden USED TO be the whole prelude
-- scheme dump, which made a #822 recurrence visible as a wall of errors here. The
-- `one-check-driver` sprint (E-1/#1115) moved this gate's driver (`check_main`) onto
-- a front door that no longer emits the folded prelude, so the golden below is now
-- just the user's own declared scheme — a #822 recurrence would NOT be caught by
-- this file unless it also breaks `h` itself. See #2033 to re-home this pin onto a
-- driver that still dumps the folded prelude.
interface H (f : Effect -> Type) where
  h : f e -> <e> Int
